    "result_text": "The full suite (the single acceptance test) is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the audit-on-create requirement for `POST /api/owners`.\n\n**New function** \u2014 `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreated.java`:\n- A single-responsibility OfficeFloor step that reads the created `Owner` via `@Val` and emits one line through the dedicated SLF4J logger named `AUDIT`, containing the owner id, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate`.\n\n**Pipeline wiring** \u2014 `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`:\n- Inserted an `audit` step between `save` and `respond` (under `govern: [ transaction ]`, like its neighbours), so it runs only after `SaveOwner` has assigned the id and the create has succeeded.\n\nI kept the audit as its own step rather than folding it into `SaveOwner` (a persistence step) or `RespondWithOwnerCreated` (a responder), so each class keeps a single responsibility. The emitted values come straight off the entity's getters, which match the JSON the test reads back (`LocalDate.toString()` gives the same ISO date as the serialized `registrationDate`).\n\nVerified output line: `AUDIT - Owner created: id=11 customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001 registrationDate=2026-09-21`, and `AcceptanceTest.coreLogsAuditOnCreate` passes (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, BUILD SUCCESS).",
